      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe better as a followup, but these were all set into properties so that they could be read later from the androidmk singleton, but that\u0027s not necessary any more since this runs during GenerateAndroidBuildActions.  It would save memory to move these into a temporary object that only exists during GenerateAndroidBuildActions so it doesn\u0027t hold on to memory after processing this  module is done.\n\nThat\u0027s harder when ModuleBase uses an interface to call back into this, as that means the data used for this has to continue to be reachable from the cc.Module after GenerateAndroidBuildActions returns.  On the other hand, using the interface allows centralizing the check for whether Kati is enabled and skipping the work to generate the data if it is not.\n\nEventually, once everything uses module proxies, I\u0027d like to free the module type memory and only keep the providers, so maybe this can be ignored until then.",
